  "limitations": [
    "Host validation is not authentication: any client that reaches the socket can send a configured Host, and reads stay unauthenticated in both WEB_AUTH_TOKEN modes.",
    "Mutating-method responses rely on AUTH.WEB.1's Origin proof; engines that send neither Origin nor Fetch Metadata on POST remain treated as non-browser clients.",
    "The browser session cookie is host-scoped, not port-scoped; another port on the same host can still overwrite it (sign-out nuisance).",
    "WEB_HOST=localhost, Docker and reverse proxies need WEB_ALLOWED_ORIGINS (and a proxy must forward the public Host); without it pages return 421.",
    "WSGI servers that derive SERVER_NAME/SERVER_PORT from Host make the default projection follow the request and must set WEB_ALLOWED_ORIGINS.",
    "A trailing-dot hostname (localhost.) is refused as malformed."
  ],
